<%#
  How far each model agrees with the baseline, and how much it would contribute.
  Locals: comparison (an EvaluationComparison).
%>
<h2 class="h4">Agreement with the baseline</h2>

<p class="text-muted small">
  The baseline defines correctness: every other model is scored by how far its
  proposals line up with the baseline's on the <em>same page</em>. The count is
  the contribution — distinct entities and relationships proposed — and the
  fraction beneath it is how many of the baseline's the run also found.
</p>

<p class="text-muted small">
  The baseline is a stand-in for truth, not truth. Where it missed something, a
  model that found it is scored as having invented it — which is why this says
  agreement rather than accuracy. Open a cell to see what the run actually said.
</p>

<h3 class="h6">Per page</h3>
<div class="table-responsive mb-3">
  <table class="table table-sm align-middle">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Page</th>
        <% comparison.models.each do |model| %>
          <th class="text-center">
            <code class="small"><%= model.model_id %></code>
            <% if model.id == evaluation.base_model_id %>
              <div><span class="badge bg-light text-dark border">baseline</span></div>
            <% end %>
          </th>
        <% end %>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% comparison.sources.each do |source| %>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <%= link_to "##{source.id}", source_path(source) %>
            <span class="small text-muted"><%= truncate(source.url.to_s, length: 40) %></span>
          </td>
          <% comparison.models.each do |model| %>
            <% cell = comparison.cell(source, model) %>
            <td class="text-center">
              <% if cell.result.nil? %>
                <span class="text-muted" title="This pair has not run">·</span>
              <% elsif !cell.run? %>
                <%= evaluation_status_badge(cell.result.status) %>
              <% else %>
                <%= link_to cell.count, skill_evaluation_result_path(cell.result) %>
                <% if comparison.identical_to_base?(source, model) %>
                  <span class="badge bg-info text-dark" title="Proposed exactly what the baseline proposed">=</span>
                <% end %>
                <% if cell.agreement %>
                  <div class="small text-muted"
                       title="Agreed with <%= cell.agreement.agreed %> of the baseline's <%= cell.agreement.agreed + cell.agreement.missed %>, and proposed <%= cell.agreement.invented %> the baseline did not">
                    <%= agreement_fraction(cell.agreement) %>
                  </div>
                <% end %>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          <% end %>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p class="text-muted small">
  A dot is a pair that has not run — not the same as a run that proposed
  nothing, which shows as 0. <span class="badge bg-info text-dark">=</span>
  marks a run that proposed exactly what the baseline proposed on that page:
  where a cheaper model is free money.
</p>

<h3 class="h6">By model</h3>
<table class="table table-sm align-middle">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Model</th>
      <th class="text-end">Agreement</th>
      <th class="text-end">Recall</th>
      <th class="text-end">Precision</th>
      <th class="text-end">Agreed</th>
      <th class="text-end">Missed</th>
      <th class="text-end">Invented</th>
      <th class="text-end">Contribution</th>
      <th class="text-end">Pages identical to baseline</th>
      <th class="text-end">Input $/Mtok</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <% comparison.rankings.each do |ranking| %>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <code><%= ranking.model.model_id %></code>
          <% if ranking.baseline %>
            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border">baseline</span>
          <% end %>
        </td>
        <% agreement = ranking.agreement %>
        <td class="text-end fw-semibold">
          <%= ranking.baseline ? content_tag(:span, "yardstick", class: "text-muted small") : agreement_percentage(agreement.f1) %>
        </td>
        <td class="text-end"><%= ranking.baseline ? "—" : agreement_percentage(agreement.recall) %></td>
        <td class="text-end"><%= ranking.baseline ? "—" : agreement_percentage(agreement.precision) %></td>
        <td class="text-end"><%= ranking.baseline ? "—" : agreement.agreed %></td>
        <td class="text-end"><%= ranking.baseline ? "—" : agreement.missed %></td>
        <td class="text-end"><%= ranking.baseline ? "—" : agreement.invented %></td>
        <td class="text-end">
          <%= ranking.total %>
          <span class="text-muted small">(<%= number_with_precision(ranking.mean_per_page, precision: 1) %>/pg)</span>
        </td>
        <td class="text-end">
          <%= ranking.baseline ? "—" : "#{ranking.pages_identical_to_base} of #{ranking.pages}" %>
        </td>
        <td class="text-end">
          <%= ranking.model.input_price_per_million ? format("$%g", ranking.model.input_price_per_million) : "—" %>
        </td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p class="text-muted small">
  Ranked by agreement, ties broken by price ascending — two models agreeing to
  the same degree are not equal if one costs twenty times the other. Agreement is
  the harmonic mean of recall and precision, so a run cannot score well by being
  either indiscriminate or timid: <strong>recall</strong> is how much of what the
  baseline found this run also found, <strong>precision</strong> is how much of
  what it proposed the baseline backed up.
</p>

<p class="text-muted small">
  Counts are summed across pages before the ratios are taken, so a sparse page
  where the baseline found two things does not weigh as heavily as a dense one
  where it found ninety. Pages the baseline did not complete are left out
  entirely — there is no truth to score against there.
</p>
